  "solution": {
    "approach": "Accept a float number and an integer k, and print the float formatted with k decimal places.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    double val;\n    int k;\n    if (scanf(\"%lf %d\", &val, &k) == 2) {\n        printf(\"%.*f\\n\", k, val);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <iomanip>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    double val;\n    int k;\n    if (cin >> val >> k) {\n        cout << fixed << setprecision(k) << val << \"\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextDouble()) {\n            double val = sc.nextDouble();\n            int k = sc.nextInt();\n            System.out.printf(\"%.\" + k + \"f\\n\", val);\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    parts = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if len(parts) >= 2:\n        val = float(parts[0])\n        k = int(parts[1])\n        print(f\"{val:.{k}f}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction main() {\n    const parts = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (parts.length >= 2) {\n        const val = parseFloat(parts[0]);\n        const k = parseInt(parts[1], 10);\n        console.log(val.toFixed(k));\n    }\n}\n\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Use dynamic precision formatting (e.g. %.*f in C or toFixed(k) in JS)."
  },
  "hints": [
    "In C, printf(\"%.*f\", k, val) specifies the precision dynamically.",
    "In Python, f'{val:.{k}f}' sets variable precision.",
    "In JavaScript, val.toFixed(k) formats to k decimal places."
  ],
